          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Travertine</h3>
          <p>
            Like limestone, travertine is calcareous and porous, with characteristic holes that drink in spills. Use a quality impregnating sealer; for kitchen and bathroom travertine where staining is a real risk, a stain-proof sealer like Dry-Treat is worth the premium. For interior travertine tile, the low-odor Aqua Mix is ideal.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Slate</h3>
          <p>
